# Scene
trueqbit with Claude (Opus 5.5), 2026-11-13: the dev/builtin/ round,
its third commit - the Purpose check, after #1618's merge (08e83adb).

# Decided
The ontocratic-reviewer, briefed with the Purpose rule alone, read the
19 Purposes against code and sqlite.org; Claude verified its findings
against the code (fts5.h:125 using_fts5<T, Cs...>, the deprecated
highlight<O> in fts5_auxiliary.h, table_xinfo in pragma_tables.h).
Purposes, old -> new:
- functions/aggregate.h: "define the built-in aggregate SQL functions."
  -> "..., and the scalar ones that share their names." (the scalar
  MAX(X,Y,...) and MIN(X,Y,...), lang_corefunc.html; core.h's
  Intention points here). Claude's lean, taken.
- dbos.h: "gather the database objects SQLite provides." -> "..., with
  their deprecated spellings." Claude's lean (b) was "with the
  functions and spellings that belong to them"; trueqbit: "Refactor" -
  #1618 moved the auxiliary functions to functions/, so only the
  deprecated FTS5 spellings remain beside the objects; Claude narrowed
  the clause, trueqbit's yes ("yes to all three").
- dbos/fts5_deprecations.h: "keep the deprecated FTS5 spellings apart."
  (false: using_fts5<T, Cs...> and highlight<O> live elsewhere) ->
  "keep apart the deprecated FTS5 spellings that overload a general
  factory of the DSL." (is_equal of ast/binary_condition.h, order_by of
  ast/order_by.h). Claude's first wording said "another module's
  factory"; trueqbit asked what "module" meant - it reads as an SQLite
  virtual table module, FTS5 being one, and as a C++20 module; reworded.
  Its Intention was false too ("keeps fts5.h ... free of the deprecated
  spellings", fts5.h:125 holds one): now it keeps fts5.h free of what
  the two need - ast/order_by.h, functions/window.h, the serializer.
  It stays in dbos/: both spellings belong to the FTS5 table.
- dbos/pragma_tables.h: "represent the rows of the table_info PRAGMA,
  as a statement and as a table-valued function." -> "represent the
  rows of the PRAGMAs SQLite offers as table-valued functions."
  (pragma.html#pragfunc). Claude leaned for "... that list a table's
  columns"; trueqbit: "we never did that just because things were
  missing, so it should stay as wide as it will hold" - TODO.md lists
  the PRAGMAs that join through make_pragma_tables().
- functions/fts5_auxiliary.h: Purpose unchanged; its Intention becomes
  the family Intention (fts5.html#auxiliary_functions), "gathered by
  builtin/functions.h", plus the hidden column of dbos/fts5.h.
- "Built-in" stays in the Purposes (finding 5): SQLite's own term -
  "built-in collating functions", "built-in VFSes", "Built-in Aggregate
  Functions"; in window.h it tells the built-in window functions from
  aggregate window functions. Claude's lean, taken.
- The other 13 Purposes stand; the reviewer confirmed each against its
  sqlite.org page.
- Written by scratchpad builtin_headers.py, keys and Purposes updated to
  match (backup builtin_headers.py.bak1).

